Sco X-1 and Cyg X-2 have many similar features in terms of their timing and spectral properties and they have almost the same upper limit for the bolometric flux (see Bradshaw, Fomalont & Geldzahler, 1999). Thus we expect that the similar mass-radius values inferred for Cyg-2 (mass =1.44\\pm 0.06, radius =9.0\\pm 0.5 km) should also be applied to Sco X-1.

